[E-RING] Error: `ring` can't prove `p + p + p = n + n`
   ╭─[ reject/ring-hypothesis-short.sw:5:71 ]
   │
 5 │ theorem tooFew (n: Nat) (p: Nat) (h: p + p = n): p + p + p = n + n := ring [h]
   │                                                                       ────┬───  
   │                                                                           ╰───── the two sides are different polynomials
   │ 
   │ Note 1: with the hypotheses `l = r` added, each times its coefficient, the left side plus every `r` against the right side plus every `l`:
   │ 
   │ Note 2: left:  3 * p + n
   │ 
   │ Note 3: right: 2 * p + 2 * n
   │ 
   │ Note 4: the left side has `p` more and `n` less
   │ 
   │ Note 5: left over: `p - n`, the goal's left minus its right, minus each coefficient times its hypothesis's `l - r`; it has to be 0
   │ 
   │ Note 6: this statement is false; a counterexample:
   │           n = 2
   │           p = 1
   │         `p + p = n` holds
   │         `p + p + p = n + n` is false:
   │           left:  3
   │           right: 4
───╯
